  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Each copy of this edition in American English was designed and hand-bound by Sebastián Barranter and Sebastián of Naranja Ediciones and printed with a single-color, risograph appliication at La Mano Ediciones studio in Santiago, Chile ..."--Wrapper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"... Displays a collection of images featuring chemtrails (and/or contrails), all of which were taken with smartphones over the course of the last 18 months, from March 2017 to October 2018. A letter towards the future, an unagreed form of speech, distinct thread outlining the space above (us). More than anything, it is an homage to the artist's mother"--Artist's website, viewed 7/8/2019.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hardbound in dark blue fabric, opens to two textblocks, one on each inner cover, each opening from the inside, outward. Preliminary pages have circular windows that allow some words on following pages to show through. There is one page with text behind each of these pages, followed by a few blank ones before the chemtrail pages mentioned in note from artist's website. Wrapped in opaque paper with publication information printed in blue.</subfield>
  </datafield>
